/-!
# Checked seed nodes for the Fi22 image words

The first two nodes reuse the already certified literal Fi22 generator maps.
The identity and the first product are then certified on all 3510 letters,
using blocks of at most 128 kernel reductions. A checked inverse of the second
node exercises the inversion interface at the same scale. These are actual
applications to the fixed `ImageWords` expressions, not external word tests.

`GeneratorActions/source/generate_seeds.py` reproduces the certificates.
Source: ATLAS F22G1-p3510B0, used for the Fi23 action in GLS3 Table 5.3u.
The remaining shared word nodes still require their own certificates.
-/

@[expose] public section
namespace Sporadic.Fischer.Fi23.CentralizerSection.ImageContainmentCertificate.GeneratorActions
open Fi22.KernelCertificate

-- Separate numerical reductions do not retain each other's elaboration caches.
set_option Elab.async false

theorem word1_represents : Represents ImageWords.word1.val fastAPacked := by
  intro x
  exact generatorA_apply_eq_fastA x

theorem word2_represents : Represents ImageWords.word2.val fastBPacked := by
  intro x
  exact generatorB_apply_eq_fastB x

